# Chat conversation
#
# The non-voice path. A customer messages in over Twilio Conversations (SMS, web chat,
# WhatsApp) and the assistant answers in text. Nothing here touches conferences or SIP;
# the assistant is driven by a per-conversation webhook rather than a live socket, and
# answers through Anthropic rather than the OpenAI realtime API.
#
# Code: controllers/event-taskrouter-post.go (handleChatReservationCreated)
#       controllers/event-conversation-post.go
#       services/artificial-intelligence/anthropic.go

title: |md
  # Chat conversation
  A customer messages in and the assistant answers in text over Twilio Conversations.
| {near: top-center}

shape: sequence_diagram

customer: Customer
conversations: Twilio Conversations
taskrouter: Twilio TaskRouter
app: zenn-ai-assistant
claude: Anthropic API

customer -> conversations: Opens a conversation (SMS, web chat, WhatsApp)
conversations -> taskrouter: A chat task is created carrying the conversationSid
taskrouter -> taskrouter: Reserves the virtual agent worker
taskrouter -> app: POST /twilio/taskrouter/event (reservation.created)

wiring: The conversation is wired to the assistant {
  app -> app: Worker attributes say isVirtualAgent and the channel is chat
  app -> taskrouter: Accepts the reservation
  app -> app: Reads the conversationSid off the task attributes
  app -> conversations: Records the taskSid on the conversation attributes

  # The task sid is stashed on the conversation because the message webhook that arrives
  # later carries only the conversation sid, and end_task needs the task.

  app -> conversations: Creates a scoped webhook to /twilio/conversation/event
  app -> conversations: Filtered to onMessageAdded, replay after 0
}

turn: Each customer message {
  customer -> conversations: Sends a message
  conversations -> app: POST /twilio/conversation/event (onMessageAdded, form encoded)
  app -> conversations: Fetches the conversation to read back the taskSid
  app -> app: Loads the active prompt configuration from Postgres
  app -> app: Builds a fresh agent for this message only

  # The agent is constructed per message and fed just this one message, so the assistant
  # carries no history between turns of the same conversation.

  app -> claude: SendMessage with the system prompt and the end_task, close_conversation tools
  claude -> app: Reply text and any tool calls
  app -> conversations: Sends the reply authored as bot
  conversations -> customer: Delivers the reply
}

echo: The reply is itself a new message {
  conversations -> app: POST /twilio/conversation/event (onMessageAdded, author bot)
  app -> app: Handled like any other message

  # Nothing distinguishes the assistant's own message from the customer's here. There is
  # no author check on the way in, and the outbound message does not set
  # X-Twilio-Webhook-Enabled to false, so the reply is delivered back to this webhook.
  # Confirm against a live conversation before relying on this diagram either way.
}

wrapup: Wrapping up {
  claude -> app: end_task tool call
  app -> taskrouter: Completes the task using the stashed taskSid
  claude -> app: close_conversation tool call
  app -> conversations: Closes the conversation
}
